WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.205
Week 11: Food, Markets, and Restaurants. buy food order a meal handle dietary needs and problems

2
00:00:07.205 --> 00:00:19.831
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can buy food, order a meal, handle dietary needs and problems. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:19.831 --> 00:00:28.017
Language system. Quantities; count and mass nouns; direct objects; polite requests with querer, poder, and quisiera.

4
00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:35.648
Sound and delivery. Single tap r and trill rr in high-frequency food and service vocabulary.

5
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:45.181
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:45.181 --> 00:01:12.185
Model language. Quisiera probar el plato del día. — I would like to try the daily special. ¿Cuánto cuesta un kilo de tomates? — How much does a kilogram of tomatoes cost? Para mí, una sopa sin carne. — For me, a soup without meat. El camarero nos trae la cuenta. — The waiter brings us the bill. Disculpe, pedí agua y no refresco. — Excuse me, I ordered water, not soda.

7
00:01:12.185 --> 00:01:22.190
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
